+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 as recorded in [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 read "Changing or cancelling a visit once booked" and was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08. That ADR closed with the convention for reopening it: narrowing the row later is a recorded owner decision carrying its own non-goal ADR.
+
+The owner made that decision on 2026-08-15, stating it verbatim at intake:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner's decision quoted in Context.
+2. **Drop NG-5 entirely,** admitting cancellation alongside correction. Rejected: the decision names cancellation as still out.
+3. **Split the row** — correction in, cancellation out (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now declines cancelling a booked visit only. Correcting a booked visit's date and its description is a requirement, recorded as REQ-VIS-003.
+
+The 2026-08-08 decision stands for NG-4 and for the cancellation half of NG-5. Nothing here reopens either.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample gains a third correction flow beside owner details and pet details, and still deletes and cancels nothing.
+- A visit is no longer immutable once booked, so the two rules the booking enforces now bind twice.
+- Cancellation remains a boundary a later request reopens only by a fresh recorded owner decision.
+- One question stays open: whether any page should offer a visible way to reach the correction. The owner deferred it to a possible follow-up request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble naming it narrowed.
+- [PRD REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the requirement the narrowing admits.
+
+## References
+
+- [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — the ADR whose NG-5 half this narrowing amends.
